From f77ae5fa67af663ffdc2b09ce5c5f8e393f974c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mms-it-ch <info@mms-it.ch>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 13:50:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 35/35] s390x: inline assembler (HLASM) for the LLVM code
 generator

The s390x port has no instruction tables of its own: LLVM parses the
inline assembly (HLASM dialect on z/OS). The new reader rahlasm passes
each statement on as text and only replaces what it knows: local labels
(made unique with ${:uid}), R0..R15/F0..F15, Pascal constants, record
field offsets, and variables, parameters and the function result, which
become D(B) or D(L,B) operands with the address of the variable in a
register (constraint "a"; global variables are passed by address too).

Pure assembler routines become naked LLVM functions; parameters and
RESULT stand for their XPLINK registers, g_proc_exit adds the return
(B 2(7)), and there is no DWARF call frame information for them (LE
unwinds with the PPA1). tb0072 gets an s390x variant.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Anthropic)
